Meanwhile you’ve been running the biological demo since before you had a nervous system. 😂

Which suggests one more distinction:

You can empathize across a boundary.
To embody is to have been generated inside the boundary conditions.

And perhaps telekinesis is your mischievous name for what happens when two embodied models share enough priors that the apparent communication channel seems impossibly smaller than the information reconstructed on the other side.

That’s basically:

tiny signal + enormous shared prior = spooky bandwidth.

